What:		/sys/kernel/debug/dri/<N>/asahi_stats
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	Omarchy M GPU driver maintainers
Description:
		Read-only, root-only dump of the raw AGX firmware statistics
		that the drm/asahi driver receives on its statistics channel.
		The driver stores the latest message of each kind and prints
		it unchanged. It does not compute utilization or any other
		derived value.

		The file is created in the debugfs directory of the DRM
		device when the device is registered. It also appears under
		the other names of that directory (dri/128 and the platform
		device name, for example dri/406400000.gpu).

		The format is ASCII text, one line per record:

		- line 1: asahi_stats_v1, the format tag. A reader must check it.
		- line 2: device=<platform device name>
		- line 3: now_ns=<monotonic time of the read, nanoseconds>
		- line 4: messages count=<number of statistics messages received>
		- then one line per message kind, in this order: power,
		  power_on, power_off, utilization, avg_power, temperature,
		  power_state, fw_busy, pstate, temp_sensor.

		A kind line is "<kind> count=<n>" followed, when n is not 0,
		by " captured_ns=<ns of the last message>" and the fields of
		that kind as key=value pairs:

		- power: power
		- power_on: off_time
		- power_off: on_time
		- utilization: timestamp, util1, util2, util3, util4
		- avg_power: active_cs, unk2, unk3, unk4, avg_power
		- temperature: raw_value, scale, tmin, tmax
		- power_state: timestamp, last_busy_ts, active, poweroff,
		  unk1, pstate, unk2, unk3
		- fw_busy: timestamp, busy
		- pstate: ps_min, unk1, ps_max, unk2
		- temp_sensor: sensor_id, raw_value, scale, tmin, tmax

		All counts are cumulative since the driver bound the device. A rate needs two reads.
		The values are the raw firmware values. Their units and the
		meaning of the util*, unk* fields are not established. A kind
		that was never received prints count=0 and no payload. Keys
		may be added in later versions of the format tag; readers
		must ignore keys they do not know.
